# circleci_url_orb_allow_list_entry (Resource)

Manages one entry in a CircleCI organization's URL orb allow list. Each entry permits pipelines in the organization to reference URL orbs whose source URL starts with the entry's `prefix`.

## Availability

**Available on CircleCI Cloud and CircleCI Server.** This resource uses the CircleCI v2 API, which both serve, so it works regardless of the provider's `deployment` setting.

## Behaviour

The API has no route that updates an existing entry, so changing any attribute replaces the entry: Terraform creates the new one and deletes the old one.

Reading an entry means listing the organization's allow list, because there is no read-one route. An entry removed outside Terraform therefore disappears from the listing and is dropped from state on the next refresh.

Keep `prefix` as narrow as you can. Any orb URL that starts with the prefix is permitted, so a prefix of `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/` allows orbs from every GitHub repository.

The `auth` value selects the credentials CircleCI uses when fetching a matching URL:

| `auth` | Used for |
| --- | --- |
| `none` | A publicly readable URL. |
| `github-oauth` | A private URL reachable with the organization's GitHub OAuth credentials. |
| `github-app` | A private URL reachable through the organization's GitHub App installation. |
| `bitbucket-oauth` | A private URL reachable with the organization's Bitbucket OAuth credentials. |

Related organization settings: `enable_private_orbs`, `enable_certified_public_orbs` and `enable_uncertified_public_orbs` on `circleci_organization_settings` control which registry orbs an organization may use. They are separate from this allow list, which covers orbs fetched from a URL.

## Example Usage

```terraform
# Allow URL orbs served from a specific GitHub path, fetched with the
# organization's GitHub App installation.
resource "circleci_url_orb_allow_list_entry" "circleci_public" {
  organization = "gh/acme"
  name         = "CircleCI-Public orbs"
  prefix       = "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CircleCI-Public/orbs/refs/heads/main/"
  auth         = "github-app"
}

# A publicly readable mirror needs no credentials. Keep the prefix as narrow as
# possible: any URL that starts with it is permitted.
resource "circleci_url_orb_allow_list_entry" "internal_mirror" {
  organization = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
  name         = "internal orb mirror"
  prefix       = "https://orbs.internal.example.com/approved/"
  auth         = "none"
}
```

